  "label": "User projected onto the woman as the speaker of the text",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the Black woman, who is depicted as the speaker of the text 'I dont like sandwiches.' The user identifies with or imagines themselves as the person expressing this preference, creating a personal identification with the subject of the mockery. This projection is reinforced by the woman's direct gaze and dismissive expression, which invites the viewer to see themselves in her position.",
